# WeddingOS — Supabase configuration (Phase 7)
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` (git-ignored) and fill in your own
# Supabase project's public values. See docs/SUPABASE_SETUP.md for the
# full step-by-step guide, including how to create a free Supabase
# project and where to find these values in the dashboard.
#
# If these variables are left unset, WeddingOS runs entirely in
# Demo / Local Mode (localStorage only, no network calls) — this is a
# supported, first-class mode, not a degraded fallback.
#
# SECURITY: only the two PUBLIC values below belong here. Never put the
# service_role key, the database password, or any other secret in a file
# that ships to the browser — the anon key is safe to expose because
# every table is protected by Row Level Security (see supabase/migrations/).

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
